/T (That afternoon, their music teacher entered the classroom carrying a stack of audition forms. "Anyone interested in participating can collect one after class." Almost every hand went up. Daniel raised both. The class burst into laughter. "You can only take one," the teacher reminded him. "I have two talents, ma'am." "You've shown neither so far." Even the teacher laughed. When the bell rang, students rushed towards the desk. Jo stayed seated. He watched the crowd for a moment before quietly walking forward. The teacher handed him a form. "I've been waiting for you to take one." He looked surprised. "You knew I would?" She smiled. "I've heard you practising after school." Jo blinked. "You have?" "The walls of the music room are thinner than you think." For the first time that day... his nervousness turned into excitement.)
