/T (Over the next few days, Jo discovered that having a crush was surprisingly exhausting. He found reasons to walk past her classroom. He suddenly became very interested in the library. He even started taking the longer route to the canteen because, according to Daniel, "destiny needed more opportunities." "You know she doesn't know you're doing all this, right?" Kiran asked one afternoon. Jo looked offended. "I'm not doing anything." Daniel raised an eyebrow. "You've walked past her classroom four times today." "I like walking." "Of course you do." Jo laughed. Maybe it was ridiculous. Maybe it was. But at sixteen, ridiculous things often felt important. And Jo was beginning to learn that sometimes, the smallest moments could make an ordinary day feel extraordinary.)
