/T (After that, things became a little easier. Jo and Ananya didn't suddenly become close. They didn't start talking every day or sitting together between classes. It was smaller than that. A smile when they passed each other in the corridor. A quiet "hi" near the library. Sometimes, a few words about class or the upcoming programme. Nothing important enough for anyone else to notice. But Jo noticed every little thing. One afternoon, he was leaving the music room when Ananya stopped him. "You're performing at the programme, right?" Jo looked at her, surprised. "Yeah." "I heard you practising." He smiled. "Was it that bad?" She laughed. "No. It was actually good." For some reason, that compliment stayed with him much longer than it should have. "Thanks," he said. Ananya smiled. "Good luck." Then she walked away. Jo stood there for a moment, smiling to himself.)
