/T (The first chord rang through the auditorium. Then another. Jo's hands slowly stopped shaking. The crowd disappeared behind the music, and for those few minutes, there was only the guitar, his voice, and the song he had practised so many times in his room. He wasn't thinking about the judges anymore. Or the teachers. Or even Ananya. He was simply enjoying the moment. When the final note faded, the auditorium filled with applause. Jo smiled and looked toward the audience. Ananya was clapping too. For some reason, that was the applause he noticed most. As he stepped off the stage, Daniel was waiting backstage. He grabbed Jo by the shoulders. "Bro!" Jo laughed. "What?" "You actually did it." Jo looked back toward the stage. "Yeah." For the first time, he understood why music had always felt like home.)
