/T (After the programme, Jo found Ananya near the side entrance of the auditorium. "Hey," she said. "Hey." She smiled. "You played really well." "Thanks. I was nervous." "I couldn't tell." Jo laughed. "I was." There was a brief silence. Then Ananya looked at the guitar hanging from his shoulder. "You really like music, don't you?" Jo nodded. "Yeah. A lot." "I could tell." She smiled once more before her friends called her from across the corridor. "I'll see you around." "Yeah. See you." She walked away. Jo watched her for a moment before turning back toward his friends. Daniel was already standing there with the biggest grin on his face. "Don't say it." "I wasn't going to." "You were." "I definitely was." Jo laughed. Maybe this was what falling in love felt like. At sixteen, he didn't know the difference yet.)
