/T (The school year moved on. Exams arrived, disappeared, and were replaced by sports days, class trips, celebrations and the countless little moments that made those years feel endless while they were happening. Jo and Ananya slowly became part of the same circle of familiar faces. They talked. They laughed. Sometimes they sat together during lunch. But nothing ever became what Jo had imagined it might. There was no confession. No grand moment. No promise that they would stay together. And strangely, Jo was okay with that. One afternoon, while the four friends sat beneath their usual rain tree, Daniel asked, "So... what happened to your great love story?" Jo smiled. "I think it's still being written." Arjun laughed. "Very poetic." Jo looked up at the branches above them. Maybe he was right. Maybe love wasn't supposed to happen just because you wanted it to. Maybe some things simply needed time. He just didn't know how much time he would need.)
