/T (The last day of school arrived before Jo was ready for it. The corridors that had once felt endless suddenly seemed smaller. The classrooms looked different without the noise of ordinary lessons, and the rain tree beneath which they had spent countless afternoons stood quietly in the summer heat. Everyone was busy signing shirts, taking photographs and promising to stay in touch. "We'll meet every weekend," Daniel announced. "Obviously," Arjun agreed. Kiran smiled. "You'll forget by next month." "We will not." They all laughed. Jo stood a little away from them, looking around the campus. There was something strange about knowing that tomorrow, he wouldn't have to come back here. No more morning assemblies. No more rushing between classes. No more waiting for the lunch bell. He had spent years wanting to leave school. Now that the moment had arrived... he wasn't sure he wanted to go. He looked at his friends and smiled. Some chapters end quietly. But the memories they leave behind never really do.)
