/T (That evening, Jo came home with a bag full of memories. Photographs. Signed shirts. A few old notebooks he would probably never open again. And a guitar pick someone had slipped into his pocket as a farewell gift. He placed everything on his bed and sat beside it. His room looked exactly the same. The guitar was still resting in the corner. For a moment, he thought about how much had changed since the first time he had picked it up. He had performed on stage. Made friends. Had his first crush. Learned what it felt like to admire someone and slowly let that feeling become a memory. But one question remained. He still hadn't found the love he had always imagined. His phone buzzed. Arjun: Tomorrow. New chapter. Jo smiled. He typed back. Jo: New city. A second message arrived. Daniel: New girls. Jo laughed. Then he looked at the guitar. Maybe Bengaluru would be different. Maybe this time... he would finally find what he had been searching for.)
