/T (Bengaluru welcomed Jo with rain. Not the gentle kind he was used to back home, but a sudden downpour that seemed to appear without warning and disappear just as quickly. He stood outside the railway station with two bags beside him, watching cars, buses and bikes move through the wet streets. Everything felt unfamiliar. The language. The roads. The crowds. Even the air felt different. His father called to check if he had reached safely. "Yes, I'm here." "Did you find your place?" Jo looked at the address saved on his phone. "Almost." "Take care." "I will." The call ended. Jo picked up his bags and looked toward the road ahead. For the first time, there was no school timetable waiting for him. No familiar classroom. No rain tree. No friends just a few steps away. Only a new city... and an entirely unwritten chapter.)
