/T (The next morning, Jo woke up to voices arguing in the kitchen. "Who finished my bread?" "I didn't!" "Then who did?" Jo opened his eyes and stared at the ceiling. For a moment, he forgot where he was. Then he remembered. Bengaluru.  New apartment.  New roommates.  New life. A smile appeared on his face. Back home, mornings had been quiet. Here, apparently, they came with arguments. He grabbed his towel and headed toward the bathroom. "Jo! You're going to be late!" He froze. "Late for what?" "College!" Jo looked at the clock. His eyes widened. "Oh, no." Within seconds, the apartment turned into chaos. Jo grabbed his bag, rushed toward the door, and barely managed to put his shoes on properly. As he stepped outside, he laughed. His new life had officially begun.)
