/T (The freedom of college also meant discovering parts of himself he had never really noticed before. Jo started spending more time with his guitar again. Some evenings, he would sit on the apartment balcony after dinner, playing quietly while the city moved below him. Cars passed. People talked. Rain came and went. Bengaluru was always awake. One night, Sameer stepped onto the balcony and leaned against the railing. "You ever get tired of playing that thing?" Jo smiled. "Not really." "What do you think about while you play?" Jo looked down at the guitar. He thought for a moment. "Usually nothing." Sameer laughed. "That's impossible." "Maybe that's why I like it." For a while, neither of them spoke. The city continued making noise below. Jo simply played. And somehow, the noise didn't bother him anymore.)
