/T (By his second year of college, Jo had settled comfortably into Bengaluru. College no longer felt unfamiliar. His roommates had become family, his friends had become part of his everyday routine, and most days followed a rhythm of classes, assignments, music and whatever plans his friends managed to create at the last minute. That Saturday was no different. "We're going out today," Aravind announced over breakfast. Jo looked up from his phone. "Where?" "Somewhere." "That's not a place." "It is if we don't tell you." Jo laughed. By noon, the four of them were already out, arguing about where to eat, making jokes about each other and taking photographs they would probably forget about in a week. For once, Jo wasn't thinking about love. He wasn't searching for anyone. He was simply enjoying an ordinary day with his friends. He had no idea that, before the day was over, someone was going to quite literally run into his life)
