/T (As their friendship grew, Jo began noticing the little things. Mouna always carried two pens because she was convinced one would stop working. She hated overly sweet coffee. She laughed whenever Jo tried to use a new sign and got it completely wrong. And whenever something mattered, she wrote it down instead of leaving it unsaid. One evening, Jo found a new page waiting in the diary. What are you afraid of? He stared at the question. Then he wrote: Losing people I love. Mouna read it quietly. After a moment, she wrote: Then don't take them for granted. Jo looked at her. For once, he had no clever reply. He simply nodded. That sentence stayed with him long after they went home)
