/T (That evening, Jo was sitting on the apartment balcony with his guitar when Aravind joined him. "You've been smiling a lot lately." Jo looked at him. "Have I?" "Yes." Jo looked back at the city. "Maybe I'm just happy." Aravind smiled. "Is there a reason?" Jo didn't answer immediately. Then he picked up his guitar. "Maybe." Aravind laughed. "That's all I'm getting?" "That's all." But after Aravind left, Jo sat quietly for a while. He thought about Mouna. The diary. Their Sundays. The little chocolate wrapper she had kept. And the way she always smiled when he tried to sign something correctly. Maybe Jo already knew what was happening. He just wasn't ready to say it out loud.)
