/T (The next few weeks passed quietly. Jo and Mouna grew closer without ever announcing that they were becoming something more. Their conversations lasted longer. Their walks became slower. The diary filled with little jokes, questions and thoughts neither of them said aloud. One evening, Mouna wrote: Do you believe people meet for a reason? Jo looked at her. "I used to." She waited. "I think I still do." Mouna smiled and wrote: Why? Jo took the pen. He thought about the staircase. The apology. The first song. The chocolate. The Sundays. Then he wrote: Because some meetings are too strange to be accidents. Mouna read it quietly. This time, she didn't smile. She simply looked at him for a long moment. And somehow, Jo understood.)
