/T (One Sunday, after Mass, Mouna asked Jo to stay back for a while. They sat on the steps outside the church. She opened the diary and wrote: What do you want your life to look like someday? Jo smiled. "I don't know." She raised an eyebrow. He laughed. "Okay, fine. Music. A good life. People I love around me." He paused. "Peace." Mouna read it carefully. Then she wrote: That sounds nice. Jo looked at her. "What about you?" She thought for a moment before writing. I want to be understood. Jo became quiet. He looked at her, then at the diary. "I think everyone wants that." Mouna smiled. But Jo knew her answer meant something more. And he wanted to understand.)
