/T (That evening, Jo sat on the apartment balcony with his guitar. He thought about everything that had changed. The boy who once imagined love through movie scenes would have never imagined this. There were no perfect introductions. No dramatic confessions. Just a staircase accident, an apology, a diary, a chocolate, and countless ordinary Sundays. Jo smiled. Maybe that was what made it real. He picked up his guitar and began to play. A message arrived on his phone. Mouna: Are you playing? Jo smiled. Jo: How did you know? Her reply came quickly. Mouna: I know you. Jo stared at those three words. Then he looked at the guitar in his hands. For the first time, they didn't feel like just words. They felt like home.)
