/T (After that Sunday, Jo began thinking about the future. Not in the way he once had. He no longer imagined some perfect love story waiting somewhere ahead. He had already found something real. Something imperfect. Something quiet. Something that had grown from a collision, a diary, a few chocolates, countless conversations, and ordinary Sundays. One evening, Mouna asked him through the diary: What happens next? Jo smiled. He looked at her for a moment before writing: I don't know. Then he added: But I hope you're there. Mouna read it slowly. She smiled. And beneath the fading evening light, Jo realized that for the first time in his life, he wasn't afraid of the future. He was looking forward to it.)
