/T (That evening, Jo returned home later than usual. He placed his guitar beside the bed and sat quietly for a while. Then he opened the drawer where he kept a few things he couldn't bring himself to throw away. Old photographs. A school wristband. The first chocolate wrapper Mouna had given back to him as a joke. And the little diary. Jo smiled. He opened it carefully. Page after page carried pieces of their story. Questions. Jokes. Apologies. Memories. He ran his fingers over the pages. Maybe this was why he didn't want some grand, perfect proposal. Their story had never been about perfect moments. It had always been about the small ones. Jo closed the diary. He finally knew what he wanted to do. And this time, he wasn't going to ask anyone else for advice.)
