1974 0 obj
<<
/Title (The diary had grown old with them. Its corners were worn, some pages had faded, and the handwriting had changed over the years. But Jo still kept it. One evening, he found Mouna reading through the old pages. She smiled when she reached the first one. Mouna. Just her name. The beginning of everything. Jo sat beside her. "You know, I still can't believe we started because I crashed into you." Mouna looked at him and laughed. She opened the diary and wrote: You were very bad at first impressions. Jo smiled. "Apparently, I improved." She looked at him for a moment. Then wrote: You did. Jo closed the diary. Some memories become stories. Others become a part of who you are. Theirs had somehow become both.)
/Dest [156 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2314 0 R
