2314 0 obj
<<
/Title (Years had passed since that Sunday. Life had become fuller and busier in ways neither of them could have imagined. There were responsibilities, work, ordinary problems and ordinary joys. But some things remained unchanged. On Sundays, whenever they could, Jo and Mouna still went to church together. Sometimes they talked. Sometimes they simply walked beside each other. And sometimes, they sat quietly in the same place where so much of their story had begun. Jo would look at her and smile. Mouna would smile back. Nothing more was needed. They had learned that love did not have to be loud to be certain. Sometimes, it was simply choosing the same person, again and again, every day.)
/Dest [155 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2499 0 R
/Next 1974 0 R
>>
endobj
