/Title (Years had passed, but some things never changed. Mouna still kept the diary. Jo still played his guitar. They still went to church together on Sundays whenever they could. And sometimes, without saying anything, they would simply sit beside each other. Jo would look at her. Mouna would look back. A smile was enough. Because after everything they had learned, they no longer needed to explain every feeling. They had learned each other's language. They had learned each other's silence. And somewhere between the words they wrote and the words they never needed to say, they had built a life together. A quiet life. A beautiful one. Their silent love.)
/Dest [154 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2514 0 R
/Next 2314 0 R
>>
endobj
