/Title (That evening, Jo and Mouna sat together in the quiet of their home. The diary rested between them. Jo opened it to a blank page. For a moment, he thought about everything they had written before. Then he picked up the pen. He wrote: I think I finally understand. Mouna looked at him. He continued: Love was never about finding someone who could hear every word. He turned the diary toward her. It was about finding someone who could understand the things you couldn't say. Mouna smiled. She took the pen and wrote beneath it: And staying long enough to learn. Jo smiled. He closed the diary. Outside, the world was still noisy. But between them, there was a silence that no longer needed to be explained. It was simply theirs. Theirs was a silent love.)
