/Title (Years later, Jo would still keep the diary. It sat safely on a shelf, its pages worn from years of being opened and read again. Sometimes Mouna would take it down and laugh at his old handwriting. Sometimes Jo would find a forgotten note tucked between the pages. Neither of them ever threw it away. It had started as a simple way to communicate. Somehow, it had become a record of everything they had built together. Jo looked at Mouna. "Do you remember what you wrote the first time?" She smiled. She knew exactly what he meant. Mouna. Just her name. The first word of a story neither of them knew they were beginning. Jo smiled. Some stories are written with words. Theirs had been written with silence)
