/Title (The next morning, life continued as it always did. There was coffee to make. Messages to answer. Places to be. Nothing about the world had changed. And yet, everything had. Jo looked at Mouna across the room. She smiled. He smiled back. No grand words. No promises that life would always be easy. Just the quiet certainty that whatever came next, they would face it together. Jo had once spent years wondering where his love story would begin. Now he understood. It had never needed a perfect beginning. It only needed two people willing to stay. And sometimes, the greatest love stories were the ones that began in silence.)
