/Title (That night, before going to sleep, Jo found the old diary on the table. He opened it to the very first page he had written in. The handwriting was uneven. The words were simple. But the memory was still clear. He smiled. Beside him, Mouna looked over. "What are you reading?" Jo closed the diary. "Nothing." She gave him a suspicious look. He laughed. "Just our beginning." Mouna smiled and rested her head against his shoulder. Jo looked at the diary one last time. Some stories begin with a perfect moment. Theirs had begun with a collision. And somehow, that was perfect enough.)
