/Title (Years later, Jo would sometimes find himself thinking about that first day. The staircase. The fallen notebook. The angry friend. The girl who hadn't said a word. He would laugh whenever he remembered how convinced he had been that love would arrive like a movie. It hadn't. It had arrived quietly. Through a diary. Through small chocolates. Through Sunday mornings. Through patience, mistakes, laughter and learning. And through someone who taught him that silence was never the absence of a voice. Sometimes, it was simply another way of speaking. Jo looked at Mouna and smiled. She smiled back. And in that moment, he knew, he had finally found the love he had been searching for.)
