/Title (By the time the audition ended, the investigation had already begun. Four sixteen-year-old boys had somehow decided that finding a girl's name required the seriousness of a criminal investigation. "So," Arjun said as they walked out of the auditorium, "what do we know?" "She's probably in tenth," Daniel said. "Probably?" "I saw the colour of her ID card." Jo looked at him. "That's your evidence?" Daniel nodded proudly. "I've worked with less." Kiran shook his head. "You've never worked." "Details." Jo laughed. They reached the staircase just as the girl walked past them. For a second, Jo considered saying something. Anything. Even a simple hello. But before he could gather the courage, she disappeared into the crowd. Daniel looked at him. "Tomorrow?" Jo sighed. "Tomorrow.")
