/Title (The audition continued around him. Someone walked onto the stage and began a dance performance. A few students near the back started whispering, earning an immediate warning glance from one of the teachers. Jo barely noticed. His attention kept drifting toward the girl three rows ahead. "Who are you looking at?" Arjun's voice suddenly appeared beside him. Jo immediately turned toward the stage. "No one." Arjun raised an eyebrow. "That was a very convincing no one." "I was just looking around." "Of course." Daniel leaned across from the other side. "What's happening?" "Nothing," Jo said. Daniel followed Jo's gaze. Then he looked back at him. A slow smile appeared on his face. "Oh." Jo frowned. "What?" "I know that look." "What look?" "The look people get right before they start doing something incredibly embarrassing." Arjun laughed. Jo shook his head. "You both are idiots." "Maybe," Daniel said, settling back into his seat. "But I'm usually right.")
